    "title": "pandas.PeriodIndex.weekofyear — pandas 3.0.5 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.PeriodIndex.weekofyear#\n\n- property PeriodIndex.weekofyear[source]#\n- The week ordinal of the year. See also \n  - `PeriodIndex.day_of_week`\n  - The day of the week with Monday=0, Sunday=6.\n  - `PeriodIndex.dayofweek`\n  - The day of the week with Monday=0, Sunday=6.\n  - `PeriodIndex.week`\n  - The week ordinal of the year.\n  - `PeriodIndex.weekday`\n  - The day of the week with Monday=0, Sunday=6.\n  - `PeriodIndex.year`\n  - The year of the period.\n Examples >>> idx = pd.PeriodIndex([\"2023-01\", \"2023-02\", \"2023-03\"], freq=\"M\") >>> idx.week # It can be written `weekofyear` Index([5, 9, 13], dtype='int64')",
